.TH MODBUS-FAKE-CLI 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
modbus-fake-cli \- console-style control session for the fake inverter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modbus-fake-cli
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
An interactive console on the
.B modbus-fake-inverter
JSON-lines control server: on connect it probes the fake and greets you
with the profile, the uptime, the clock and the battery state; the prompt
shows the connected port (\fBfake-inverter:5502 >\fR). TAB completes
commands, settings and their values (the listings split into
[settings]/[values]/[system] with aligned descriptions); \fB?\fR prints
the same in any position; \fBhelp <setting>\fR explains one; \fBshutdown\fR
asks \fBProceed with shutdown? [confirm]\fR first.
.PP
While idle the session sends wire pings every 55 s; when the connection
dies, the console retries (default 3 times, 10 s apart) and resumes on the
first success. The session is audited with the \fBCLI\fR prefix; the wire
commands are audited once, by the server.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-control-port " TARGET"
the control target: a unix socket path or a TCP port. Default
\fB/tmp/fake-inverter-\fR\fI<modbus-port>\fB.socket\fR; the
\fBFAKE_CTL\fR environment variable is the same knob.
.TP
.BI \-\-control-token " TOKEN" ", " \-\-control-token-file " FILE"
the token for TCP control (mutually exclusive).
.TP
.BI \-\-reconnect " N"
connection-loss retries before giving up. Default \fB3\fR;
\fB0\fR = die on loss.
.TP
.BI \-\-reconnect-wait " S"
seconds between retries. Default \fB10\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " S"
wire timeout, seconds. Default \fB5\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-audit-log " FILE|\-"
the console's own audit trail
(\fB~/.local/state/fake-inverter/audit.log\fR by default).
.TP
.BI \-\-audit-max-mb " N ", \-\-audit-files " N"
the file sink's gated rotation (defaults \fB10\fR / \fB3\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-no-audit-log
disable the console's audit trail.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FAKE_CLI_KEEPALIVE
idle ping interval, seconds (default \fB55\fR); \fB0\fR = off.
.TP
.B FAKE_CTL ", " FAKE_CONTROL_TOKEN
the default control target and TCP token.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
the session ended cleanly.
.TP
.B 1
connection or control error.
.TP
.B 2
command-line misuse.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR modbus-fake-inverter (1),
.BR modbus-fake-ctl (1)
